From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 11:19:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msxml3: Report DTD validation errors where the reader meets
 them, as Windows does.

Windows validates against the DTD as it reads and reports the first
error it meets, where the reader is then (tools/msxmlmoreprobe in the
wine-altars repository, 26 documents, MSXML 3.0 and 6.0): at the end of
the start tag of an element that may not come where it is, is not
declared, or has attributes it may not have or lacks some, in that
order; at the start of text that may not be where it is, even spaces in
an element declared EMPTY; at the name in the end tag of an element
that lacks children, XML_EMPTY_NOT_ALLOWED with none, else
XML_ELEMENT_NOT_COMPLETE; and at the end of the document for an IDREF
to no ID, with no offset and no line text.  Those are the positions the
reader's own locator gives for its startElement, characters and
endElement.

Wine validates the parsed tree with libxml2, which reports errors in
another order and where none of these are, so the reader's positions
are now kept on the nodes, every error libxml2 raises is placed at the
event it is about and the first in reading order is kept.  The
content model tells a child that may not come from children missing.
Values of attributes of a type that is one name are read as Windows
reads them: more than one name, or one starting with a character no
name starts with, have their own codes, and an ID given twice its own.

validate() names the same error at no position.  Only one case still
differs: MSXML 6.0 keeps the spaces in an element declared EMPTY and
validate() then finds them, where Wine leaves them out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

